Batch 1 of the WI-tusad campaign: inventory, enforcement, shared arity.
No language producer is migrated here.

Gate: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_id_floor_gate.py runs the
full pipeline over 79 per-language fixtures, each carrying an earlier
same-name sibling (overload, clause, same-name function in another scope),
then again with that sibling deleted. It ratchets, against the shrink-only
.ci/stable-id-floor-baseline.json, (1) the per-(language, kind) count of
callable/member records whose stable_id is the ADR-0035 backstop floor key
or null, and (2) the set of languages where the deletion moved, nulled or
dropped another symbol's id. Growth and shrink both fail, so each migration
ratchets its rows down in the same PR. Baseline: 38 languages, 67 floor +
43 null; 38 languages fail the deletion check (incl. producer-computed
cpp/hlsl/nim/ada/pascal/sql overload ties and line-hashed pony/scss/twig).
The gate functions live in the test module: WI-ratuv forbids new
production functions with test-only callers. coverage-only-deps maps the
78 analyzer files and base.py to the gate.

Shared arity: overload_arity.declared_arity / declared_arity_stable_id
derive a callable's ADR-0035 id from meta["parameters"] (or a bare
meta["arity"]) for grammars where compute_stable_id finds no params node;
untyped values equal compute_stable_id's for the same parameters, typed
tier when a parameter declares a type. behaviours.callback_stable_id now
mints through it, byte-identically (pinned).

Refs WI-tusad-rilub-jipuv-tibum-rijab-tahut-kijov-toral

